            <span class="rp-label" style="color:#4ade80">Time Saved</span>
            <div class="rp-value" id="sp-saved" style="color:#4ade80">—</div>
            <div class="rp-sub" id="sp-pct">vs listening at 1x</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="result-note" style="margin-top:16px" id="sp-note"></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <h2>What is the Libby speed calculator?</h2>
  <div class="lsc-answer">
    <span class="aa-label">Direct Answer</span>
    <p>The Libby speed calculator is a free tool that finds the minimum playback speed you need to finish a <a href="https://libbyapp.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Libby</a> audiobook before your library loan expires. Enter your remaining book length, days left, and daily listening hours - the calculator shows your minimum speed and whether 1x, 1.5x, or 2x is fast enough.</p>
  </div>
  <p>Libby loans run for 7 to 21 days depending on your library. Most audiobooks are 8 to 15 hours long. If you cannot listen every day or can only listen for 1 hour per day, you may need to increase your playback speed to finish in time.</p>
  <p>The calculator also includes a basic speed tab for any Libby audiobook - enter the original length and your playback speed to get your exact adjusted listening time and time saved.</p>
  <h2>What speed should I use if my Libby loan expires soon?</h2>
  <div class="lsc-answer">
    <span class="aa-label">Direct Answer</span>
    <p>Use the loan deadline calculator above to find your exact required speed. The formula is: Minimum Speed = Book Length / (Days Left x Hours Per Day). If your loan expires in 3 days and you can listen 2 hours per day, you have 6 hours available. An 8-hour book at 6 available hours requires a minimum of 1.34x speed.</p>
  </div>
  <p>Standard speed recommendations when your Libby loan is expiring:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>7+ days remaining:</strong> 1x to 1.5x is sufficient for most audiobooks</li>
    <li><strong>3 to 6 days remaining:</strong> 1.5x to 2x recommended for books over 10 hours</li>
    <li><strong>1 to 2 days remaining:</strong> 2x to 3x required depending on book length and hours available</li>
    <li><strong>Loan expires today:</strong> Calculate your exact minimum speed using the Deadline Calculator above</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Use the <a href="/">main audiobook speed calculator</a> if you want to calculate adjusted times across all speeds side-by-side without the deadline constraint.</p>
  <h2>How do I finish a Libby audiobook before the loan expires?</h2>
  <div class="lsc-answer">
    <span class="aa-label">Direct Answer</span>
    <p>To finish a Libby audiobook before the loan expires: (1) calculate your minimum required speed using the tool above, (2) set that speed in the Libby app under Settings &gt; Playback Speed, (3) schedule fixed listening sessions each day, (4) if the required speed exceeds 2x, request a loan extension first.</p>
  </div>
  <p>The two biggest factors that determine whether you can finish are your available hours per day and the remaining book length. Increasing speed is effective up to 2x for most listeners - above 2x, comprehension decreases and you may need to re-listen to sections, which wastes more time than the speed saves.</p>
  <div class="lsc-callout tip">
    <h4>Best Strategy for Expiring Loans</h4>
    <p>If the calculator shows you need above 2x, check if your library allows early renewal first. Many Libby libraries allow renewal 3 days before expiry if no holds are waiting - this is faster than trying to rush through at 2.5x or 3x speed.</p>
  </div>
  <p>For a full step-by-step guide, see <a href="/how-to-finish-libby-audiobook-before-loan-expires/">How to Finish a Libby Audiobook Before the Loan Expires</a>.</p>
  <h2>What is the maximum playback speed on Libby?</h2>
  <div class="lsc-answer">
    <span class="aa-label">Direct Answer</span>
    <p>The maximum playback speed on Libby is 3x. Libby supports speeds from 0.5x to 3x in 0.1x increments - 26 speed options total. At 3x speed, a 10-hour audiobook takes 3 hours 20 minutes. At 2.5x, it takes 4 hours. At 2x, it takes exactly 5 hours. Libby's maximum of 3x is lower than Audible's 3.5x maximum.</p>
  </div>
