  </table>
  <p>For full documentation on Libby's speed settings, see the <a href="https://help.libbyapp.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">official Libby help center</a>.</p>
  <h2>How does Libby playback speed compare to Audible?</h2>
  <div class="lsc-answer">
    <span class="aa-label">Direct Answer</span>
    <p>Libby supports 0.5x to 3x speed in 0.1x increments. Audible supports 0.5x to 3.5x in 0.05x increments. Audible has a higher maximum speed (3.5x vs 3x) and finer control (0.05x vs 0.1x steps). Libby is free via library card; Audible requires a paid subscription. For listeners who regularly use 3x or above, Audible is the better platform.</p>
  </div>
