  </table>
  <p>For a full side-by-side breakdown, see <a href="/libby-vs-audible-speed-comparison/">Libby vs Audible Speed Comparison</a>.</p>
  <h2>How do I change the playback speed on Libby? (Step-by-step)</h2>
  <div class="lsc-answer">
    <span class="aa-label">Direct Answer</span>
    <p>To change speed on Libby: open your audiobook → tap the screen to show controls → tap the speed icon (shows "1x" by default) in the bottom control bar → tap your desired speed from the list. The speed setting saves automatically per book. Changes take effect immediately without losing your place.</p>
  </div>
  <ol>
    <li>Open the Libby app and start your audiobook</li>
    <li>Tap anywhere on the screen to reveal the playback controls</li>
    <li>Tap the speed button — it shows your current speed (default: 1x)</li>
    <li>Tap the speed you want from the list (0.5x to 3x)</li>
    <li>The new speed applies instantly — your place is not affected</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="lsc-callout">
    <h4>Speed Resets Between Sessions?</h4>
    <p>Libby saves your speed setting per book, not globally. If you switch to a different audiobook, your speed may reset to 1x. You need to set your preferred speed separately for each audiobook you borrow.</p>
  </div>
  <p>Download the <a href="https://libbyapp.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Libby app</a> for iOS or Android if you have not already connected your library card.</p>
  <h2>What happens to my Libby audiobook when the loan expires?</h2>
  <div class="lsc-answer">
    <span class="aa-label">Direct Answer</span>
    <p>When a Libby loan expires, the audiobook is automatically returned and removed from your app. Your listening progress is not saved unless you had previously synced. You can place a new hold on the title immediately after return. If no holds are waiting, many libraries allow renewal 3 days before expiry.</p>
  </div>
  <p>Three things to do before your Libby loan expires:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Use the deadline calculator above to find the minimum speed needed to finish in time</li>
    <li>Check if your library allows early renewal (available 3 days before expiry for most libraries)</li>
    <li>Place a hold on the title now so it returns to you faster if you cannot finish</li>
  </ul>
  <p>For more detail on Libby loan rules and how long you can borrow, see <a href="/how-long-can-you-keep-libby-audiobook/">How Long Can You Keep a Libby Audiobook?</a></p>
