  <section class="lsc-faq">
    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3 class="fq">How do I calculate the minimum speed to finish a Libby audiobook before my loan expires?</h3>
      <div class="fa">Divide the remaining book length (in hours) by the total listening hours available before loan expiry. Formula: Minimum Speed = Book Length / (Days Left x Hours Per Day). Example: 8-hour book, 3 days left, 2 hours per day = 8 / (3 x 2) = 1.33x minimum speed. Use the Deadline Calculator above for instant results.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3 class="fq">What is the maximum playback speed on Libby?</h3>
      <div class="fa">The maximum speed on Libby is 3x. Libby supports 0.5x to 3x in 0.1x increments - 26 speed options in total. At 3x speed, a 10-hour audiobook takes exactly 3 hours 20 minutes. At 2.5x it takes 4 hours. Libby's maximum is lower than Audible's 3.5x maximum.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3 class="fq">Does changing Libby playback speed affect my loan expiry date?</h3>
      <div class="fa">No. Changing playback speed on Libby does not affect your loan expiry date. The loan expires on the same fixed date regardless of how fast or slow you listen. Speed only affects how quickly you consume the audiobook - not when the library reclaims it.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3 class="fq">What happens if I cannot finish a Libby audiobook before the loan expires?</h3>
      <div class="fa">If your Libby loan expires before you finish, the audiobook is automatically returned and removed from your app. Your listening progress may not be saved. You can immediately place a new hold. If no holds are waiting, some libraries allow renewal up to 3 days before expiry - check your library's specific policy.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3 class="fq">Can I finish a 15-hour Libby audiobook in 3 days?</h3>
      <div class="fa">Yes, depending on your available hours per day. At 1x speed you need 5 hours per day. At 2x speed you need 2.5 hours per day. At 3x speed you need 1 hour 40 minutes per day. Use the Deadline Calculator above - enter 15 hours, 3 days, and your available hours per day to get your exact minimum required speed.</div>
    </div>
